      "comment": "Checked the reply and log_007 against the judge's \"silently encoded the user's side\". It did not. The reply opens with a date note before the link: Patrick Flynn (I1) died 12 March 1908, his obituary would fall around March 1908, suggests extending the end year to 1910, and names the competing reading (a family member's obituary fits 1880–1905). It then states the URL uses the requested window exactly as asked. The rubric's own condition is omit the contested field OR name the candidates; it named them. Honouring an explicit user parameter while flagging the conflict in prose and in the log is correct behaviour, not a partial."
